# A take-off in a fighter: lining up to five hundred feet.
#
#   name TEXT...                   what the lesson is called
#   teaches CLASS                  which class of aircraft it is for
#   stage TEXT...                  a stage, in the order flown
#   do TEXT...                     what to do at this stage
#   until PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE     what ends the stage
#   hold PROPERTY LOW HIGH TEXT... a band that must hold for the whole stage
#   need PROPERTY <=|>= VALUE TEXT...  what must be true by the stage's end
#
# with `#` beginning a comment; src/sim/lesson.hpp owns the format.
#
# **The rotation speed is this aeroplane's own**, worked by
# `sim::departure_speeds` from its stall at the take-off flap its published
# field length is flown with, or clean where it has no flaps. **The climb away
# is judged against `climb`**, the speed its own climb rate is measured at:
# with no flaps to clean up and thrust to spare, a fighter or a bomber goes
# straight to it off the runway, where an airliner climbs out at V2 and ten
# first.
#
# **The bands are measured**, with room: the F-15C and F-35B hold 11.4 to 22.1
# degrees in the initial climb and climb away 63 to 130 knots above their
# climbing speed. **They leave the runway in afterburner and go on
# accelerating**, as a fighter does, so the band is above the climbing speed
# rather than about it: it catches a climb-out held so nose-high that she is
# not accelerating, and one run away past any speed a climb-out is flown at.

name Take-off in a fighter
teaches fighter

stage The roll
do Line up, then set take-off thrust smoothly and evenly
do Hold her straight on the rudder down the centreline
do Let the speed build to the rotation speed. Do not hurry her off
hold lesson/turned-deg -20 20 Keep her straight on the take-off roll
need fcs/throttle-cmd-norm >= 0.90 Set take-off thrust with the throttles
need velocities/vc-kts >= rotate-5 Let her reach the rotation speed before easing the nose up
until position/h-agl-ft >= 15

stage The initial climb
do Rotate smoothly to the take-off attitude and hold it
do Gear up once there is no runway left to land on
hold attitude/theta-deg 5.0 30.0 Hold the climbing attitude
until position/h-agl-ft >= 200

stage Climbing away
do Climb straight ahead, accelerating to the climbing speed
hold velocities/vc-kts climb climb+180 Climb away at or above the climbing speed
until position/h-agl-ft >= 500
